Use `ConfigureLifecycleEvents` in `MauiProgram.cs`:

```csharp
builder.ConfigureLifecycleEvents(events =>
{
#if ANDROID
    events.AddAndroid(android => android
        .OnPause(activity => { /* app losing focus */ })
        .OnStop(activity => { /* app fully backgrounded */ }));
#elif IOS || MACCATALYST
    events.AddiOS(ios => ios
        .DidEnterBackground(app => { /* app backgrounded */ }));
#endif
});
```

**Key points:**

- Android `OnPause` maps to the cross-platform `Deactivated` event (lost focus, may still be visible). `OnStop` maps to `Stopped` (fully backgrounded).
- iOS `DidEnterBackground` maps to `Stopped`.
- If you don't need platform-specific APIs, you can use the cross-platform equivalent instead — override `OnStopped()` on your `Window` subclass, which fires on both platforms when the app backgrounds.

**Cross-platform alternative:**

```csharp
protected override Window CreateWindow(IActivationState? activationState)
{
    var window = base.CreateWindow(activationState);
    window.Stopped += (s, e) => { /* runs on all platforms */ };
    return window;
}
```

**Pitfall:** On Android, the back button can skip `Stopped` and go straight to `Destroying`, so also save critical state in `OnDestroying` or the Android `.OnDestroy()` hook.
